# The buried oxide is the thermal resistance to the substrate: a thicker one makes the shifter more efficient and slower.
# Reference: the same mesh solved with a sparse direct solver in SciPy.
title Buried oxide 1 um thick
grid dx=0.25 dy=0.25
window width=60 ymin=-10 ymax=4
layer si -10 0
layer sio2 0 4
rect si -0.25 0.25 1 1.25
rect tin -1 1 3 3.25
heater h xmin=-1 xmax=1 ymin=3 ymax=3.25 power=0.1
probe wg xmin=-0.25 xmax=0.25 ymin=1 ymax=1.25
expect response wg h 109.834304 1e-7
expect pi_power wg h 37.9359317 1e-7
expect peak 36.2308433 1e-7
expect balance 1e-9
expect cells 13440
